TunaOS branding — third-party sources

The files in marks/ and wordmarks/ are copies from tuna-os/tunaOS:

  marks/<variant>.svg       <- system_files/usr/share/tunaos/logos/<variant>.svg
  marks/tunaos.svg          <- system_files/usr/share/pixmaps/tunaos.svg
  wordmarks/<variant>.svg   <- system_files/usr/share/tunaos/lettermarks/<variant>.svg
  wordmarks/<variant>-dark.svg
                            <- system_files/usr/share/tunaos/lettermarks/<variant>-dark.svg

The generator is scripts/branding/make-lettermarks.py in tuna-os/tunaOS.
It is the source of truth. Do not edit these copies by hand.

Emoji marks
  The marks in marks/ and the mark inside each wordmark are glyphs from
  Noto Emoji (https://github.com/googlefonts/noto-emoji).
